Chitala H0.1, N1.6 on the GICv2 board: the WFI experiment's "after"
(native/spike/run-n1.6-wfi.sh). On qemu_virt_aarch64, seL4 no longer traps a
guest's WFI and WFE, as on qemu_virt_aarch64_gicv3 (microkit-0003). Nothing
else changes. scripts/build-sdk.sh applies it only for
N1_SDK_VARIANT=gicv2-no-wfi-traps, in an SDK of its own: never to the board
of the released SDK, nor to the SDK the other steps use.

--- a/build_sdk.py
+++ b/build_sdk.py
@@ -298,16 +298,19 @@
         name="qemu_virt_aarch64",
         arch=KernelArch.AARCH64,
         gcc_cpu="cortex-a53",
         loader_link_address=0x70000000,
         smp_cores=4,
         kernel_options={
             "KernelPlatform": "qemu-arm-virt",
             "QEMU_MEMORY": "2048",
+            # Chitala H0.1, the WFI experiment's "after" (native/spike/sdk/wfi):
+            # a guest's WFI/WFE run on the CPU instead of trapping to its VMM
+            "KernelArmDisableWFIWFETraps": True,
             # There is no peripheral timer, so we use the ARM
             # architectural timer
             "KernelArmExportPTMRUser": True,
         },
     ),
     # Chitala N1 (native/spike/sdk): QEMU virt with a GICv3, which the Hermit
     # kernel needs; otherwise as qemu_virt_aarch64. Run with
     # -machine virt,virtualization=on,gic-version=3.
